<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Is Isaiah Collier on a Rookie Contract?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Collier is paid <strong>$2.76m</strong> because the rookie scale pays by pick number, and the 29th pick is near the bottom of the first round.</p>
<ul>
<li>He went 29th in 2024 out of USC after one season.</li>
<li>All four years are worth <strong>$12.9m</strong>, and the first three are guaranteed.</li>
<li>Utah exercised the option on this season in October 2025.</li>
<li>A second option covers 2027-28.</li>
<li>He earns about a fifth of what the second pick from 2026, Darryn Peterson, does at the same club.</li>
</ul>
<p>He has never been paid by another club.</p>

